	- Skip the first part
		=> ending
	- Read it
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You are ready. Ask what you wish!
	Brian: I wish to know, why did the house target me, Margaret, Alice, and Dan? What did we do to deserve such a fate?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You were scared.
	Brian: What?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The house feeds on the fear of disorientation. You were scared to go in. But drawn to your fate.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: If you weren't scared, it would not have bothered.
	Brian: And why then did it let ME leave while EVERYONE else died??
	IPR1-HY-NOB: To feed on you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Look at yourself. You still fear it, you still feed it.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: All the others would have slowly moved on.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: But instead, you are drawn deeper, by the guilt.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: It may claim you eventually. But it will savor your paranoia for a long time before that happens.
	Brian: [Heavy breathing]
	Brian: Ok... ok... fine... Then, how do I save them? How do I save them from that house!
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You can't.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: There is no way to save someone in the house.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You cannot save them.
	Brian: What... no...
	IPR1-HY-NOB: There is not even enough of them left to save.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Take Alice. Do you know what state she is in right now?
	Brian: No, please, I don't want to know.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Oh... but you do... I can sense your curiosity... and fear.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She no longer feels the stare of the mirror's gaze.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: No, instead she is the mirror.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Twisted and bent like a funhouse show, endlessly shattered and contorted.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And she is mad. Mad but scared. And in so much pain.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She cannot remember how she got there. But she remembers you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The twisted figure that pretended to be her friend.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: That brought her to her doom.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: That lied that it would rescue her.
	Brian: [Sobbing] I beg you, no more.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Or, how about Margaret?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She still sits on those stairs.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She was one to go quickly.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Despite the twisting, she still feels the height she is at.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And she refuses to look down.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Even though it might be up.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She goes down and down the stairs.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Sometimes, she feels like she is standing in place, and the stairs walk her.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And sometimes, she remembers a shadow. A heinous reminder of why she is there. You.
	Brian: [In tears] Please. I did not ask for this.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Oh, but you did.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You cannot lie to me, Brian.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: I know. And you know I won't lie to you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Not like you did to poor Dan.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: "We go together."
	IPR1-HY-NOB: He is still there.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Still searching for you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Still partially sane.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Sometimes, he thinks you went ahead and he fell behind.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Sometimes, he thinks you found a door, but it locked behind you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And sometimes, he thinks the hallway ate you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: But he remembers the promise.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And so he keeps searching, calling for one who he will never see.
	Brian: [On the verge of breakdown] Fine, you monster.
	Brian: If I cannot save them, how do I avenge them?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Oh... you can't.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The house will exist as long as it is feared.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And it has plenty of victims thanks to you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: It can stretch their misery for centuries.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And even so, as long as you live, it can always feast on you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And those unfortunate enough to open a door meant for you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You cannot avenge them.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And you will help perpetuate the thing that killed them.
	Brian: [Broken] Fine. Fine.
	Brian: If that's how it is, how do I save myself?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You can't...
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You are marked by the house.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: It's only a matter of time before it swallows you too.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: But don't get your hopes up.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The guilt will not leave you.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Only grow worse.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You will never find peace.
	Brian: [Broken] Why?? Why can't you offer any hope or help?
	Brian: What did I do to you to torment me so?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: I am only doing what you wanted.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You wanted to know the truth.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: I tell only the truth.
	Brian: I... no... there must be... something...
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You know I am truthful. And you know there is no hope.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Goodbye, Brian.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Feel free to come again if any more questions arise.
	=> ending
else:
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You did not read enough.
=> END

